n also pass  a callback which just means a function  to run as soon as if we get the data  okay I just paste it in this here okay  we're gonna load the text as we did  before but now afterwards we're gonna  run this callback function in the  callback function we have the response  text status text and the xhr  so if the status text equals success  that just means we've successfully  gotten the data and then we can alert  external content loaded successfully if  this dashed x equals err we can alert  what the air was you're always going to  get some kind of response after you you  try to do an ajax call a lot of things  can go wrong with Ajax so you usually  want to set up something that will  happen if there's an error like would  you hear let's see an example of that so  it's going to say external content  loaded successfully and it's going to  load the content now if I change this  website to something that doesn't exist  I'm just going to add a 1 in here and  now let's see what happens when I click  the button err 404 not found so that's  what we're getting this error message  down here okay I'm gonna comment all  this out again and we're gonna add  another line at the top here I'm going  to show you something similar to the  Ajax load command but this is get just  like the load method get' is going to  get data from a server the main  difference is that load is going to load  the data directly into an element and  get is not necessarily going to load  that data into an element here we have  the get method is just dollar sign dot  get and then we're going to pass in what  we're gonna get so the same website from  before and then we have the callback  function this text is not loaded  anywhere so in the callback function  we're going to have to say what's going  to happen to the text in this case we're  just going to console dot log so you can  see in the callback function we have the  data and the status we're showing that  right here the data is going to equal  